accepts - acceptance probe for the document-signing appliance
============================================================

    accepts FILE

Reads one CMS ContentInfo object and writes this appliance's verdict for it,
and nothing else, to stdout:

    accept              the object is accepted
    reject <offset>     the object is not accepted; <offset> is the byte
                        offset, within FILE, of the tag octet of the first
                        element this appliance does not tolerate

Exit status is 0 for accept, 1 for reject, 2 on a usage or I/O error.

The verdict is this appliance's own.  It is the same code path the signing
appliance runs before it stores a lab report, so it, and not any other tool,
decides what the appliance will and will not take.  The desktop validator
kept in vendor_notes/ is a different program and does not necessarily agree
with it.
